WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:01.801
The details that we're getting.

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.937
Do not answer the big questions.

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:06.006
What exactly it is?

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:08.775
Who is the owner of this object?

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:10.744
Considering that they knew about it

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:11.644
last night,

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:12.879
only shot it down

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:14.047
less than 2 hours ago,

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:16.082
and they have not yet retrieved that.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.550
Should we know more now?

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.653
Should they know more than they do

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:22.989
Well, Victor, in this particular case,

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:24.057
probably not.

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:25.725
You know, there's always the fog of war,

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:26.459
and in this case,

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:27.861
the fog of the incident.

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.896
And what we're dealing with

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:32.165
is a situation where

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:34.467
in the wake of the balloon incident

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:37.570
that happened just

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.105
six days ago or so.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:40.573
So now we're looking at something

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:41.941
that's very,

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:43.777
you know, perhaps a little bit different,

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:44.911
but somewhat similar.

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:46.846
And we're out of an abundance

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:49.049
of political caution.

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:52.652
The craft was was taken out

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.721
because it posed.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.423
General Ryder said it posed a threat

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:59.659
to civilian aircraft and could possibly

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:00.760
have also been

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.063
some type of a collection platform.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:04.531
We don't know that yet,

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:05.799
but they decided

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:06.733
they didn't want to take the

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:07.667
chance again.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:08.935
And as a result,

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.703
we have what we have at the moment.

00:01:12.172 --> 00:01:12.539
Kelly

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:14.040
Atwood, to you,

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.142
the question of who's responsible.

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:18.845
The words that still stick with me

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:19.946
are from John Kirby.

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:20.313
And he said,

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:23.416
I have no idea who owns this.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.251
What do you know about the efforts

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:26.419
happening right now

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:28.655
potentially to find that out?

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:30.123
Of course, the first country

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.991
that most people think of is China,

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:33.093
considering that balloon

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:34.260
that just passed over the U.S.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.895
a couple of days ago.

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:37.097
Yeah, that's right.

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:38.865
I mean, I would

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:40.033
think it's fair to say that

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.968
there is a widespread effort

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.870
to figure out where this came from

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.972
and who owns it, because as you said,

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:46.239
you know,

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:47.140
multiple officials

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.408
saying today from the White House

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:49.642
and from the Pentagon, the U.S.

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.544
doesn't know if this is state owned

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:53.446
or if this is privately owned.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:54.314
So they're really trying

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:55.849
to figure out who owns this

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:56.883
and where it came from

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:58.084
because they first detected

00:01:58.084 --> 00:02:00.420
it just yesterday when it came close

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.522
and then into U.S. airspace.

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:03.490
I do think that

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:04.257
there's one

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:06.192
significant thing to point out here,

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:06.993
which is that

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.194
with the Chinese spy

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.830
balloon, there was a number of contacts

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.031
between U.S.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.167
diplomats and Chinese diplomats

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:17.337
before the Biden administration took

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:18.705
the move to shoot it down

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:20.607
off the coast of South Carolina.

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:21.908
The fact that there hasn't

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:24.077
been any back and forth with China,

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:25.211
according to the White House

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:25.845
on this, does

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:26.880
indicate

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:27.847
that perhaps

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:29.415
they don't think it is

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:30.383
Chinese owned,

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:31.584
but of course, they aren't

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:33.653
counting out anything right now.

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:35.321
And what we'll be watching for

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:37.290
is the contacts, particularly

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:40.894
on the diplomatic front, to inform allies

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:42.095
about what happened here

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:44.364
and try and work with Five Eyes.

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:45.064
Those are partners

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:46.499
that we share intelligence

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:47.700
with to figure out

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.302
what those countries might know

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:50.403
that could help us.

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:51.371
In addition

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:53.206
to what's going to be

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:54.641
this effort on the ground,

00:02:54.641 --> 00:02:56.943
this obviously went down over

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.546
this was over frozen water.

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:01.080
So it's going to be a very different

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.148
excavation effort.

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:04.184
But that will probably be their best shot

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:05.418
at figuring out the answers

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:06.352
to many of these questions.

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:07.921
We don't know right now.

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:09.556
Let's bring in Oren Liebermann,

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:10.590
our Pentagon correspondent,

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.058
who was there in the briefing

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:13.760
or in the Pentagon,

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:14.661
also at the White House.

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:15.195
They're

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:19.165
very careful not to describe this balloon

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:19.899
and part,

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:20.767
as General Ryder said,

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:23.002
simply because he does not know.

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.070
But we're learning

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.573
that is not similar in size or shape.

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:28.675
To that Chinese surveillance balloon

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:30.543
that was shot down last week.

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:31.411
What stood out to you

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:32.312
from what we just heard

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:33.613
from the Pentagon?

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:34.113
Correct.

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:35.281
Significant differences

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:37.083
simply in how they describe this.

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:38.318
Obviously, we said many times

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:39.219
the previous object

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:41.020
was about the length of three busses,

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.122
the balloon itself, some 200 feet tall,

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:44.490
nothing near that size

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.458
in terms of the object

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:46.593
that was shot down.

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:47.126
And Pentagon

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:47.760
Press Secretary

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:48.661
Brigadier General Pat

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:49.762
Ryder was very careful

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.197
not to describe this in any way

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:52.265
other than saying

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:55.235
it was about a small car sized object

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:56.769
and that it was unmanned.

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.204
There wasn't much beyond that

00:03:58.204 --> 00:04:00.273
in terms of how it was moving.

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:01.741
Did it have any sort of propulsion

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.276
or any sort of maneuverability?

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:04.978
So there are obviously a tremendous

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:05.778
number of questions

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.213
in what this was,

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:08.681
frankly, what it looked like,

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:10.116
despite the fact that U.S.

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:11.551
fighter jets and fighter pilots

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:13.019
had eyes on this

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:14.387
since it was first spotted

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:15.989
and then what it was doing right

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:18.024
at the end of the press conference,

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:19.292
the Pentagon said it was moving

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:21.027
in a northeasterly direction.

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:22.495
It had been spotted yesterday

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:24.130
and they'd kept an eye on it since then.

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.465
Eventually, the decision was made

00:04:25.465 --> 00:04:26.199
to shoot it down.

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:29.068
It had been roughly at the same altitude

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:30.069
throughout the time the U.S.

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:30.870
had eyes on it.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.405
So at about 40,000 feet,

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:33.306
which is roughly

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:35.275
the upper edge of commercial air traffic,

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:36.309
and that Brigadier

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:36.876
General Pat

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:37.410
Ryder said, is

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.178
why the decision was ultimately made

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:40.346
to shoot this down.

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:42.715
One of the key questions we asked is

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:43.349
the Pentagon

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:45.351
made a big point of this rider himself

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:46.786
and others as well,

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:48.254
that there was a benefit

00:04:48.254 --> 00:04:50.156
to having the other balloon fly

00:04:50.156 --> 00:04:51.557
across much of the continental

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:52.158
United States

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:54.160
in terms of intelligence gathering.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:55.295
If that's the case,

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:57.330
why was this one shot down so quickly

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:58.931
before there was any attempt

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:00.033
at intelligence gathering?

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:01.467
Because the Pentagon described him

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:02.368
in great terms

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:03.102
how much intelligence

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:05.071
they gained from the previous balloon.

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:05.672
In this case.

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:06.105
The Pentagon

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:07.840
simply said that every decision

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.342
on every individual object

00:05:09.342 --> 00:05:10.677
or every scenario like this

00:05:10.677 --> 00:05:12.812
will be decided on an individual basis.

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:13.880
And in this case, partially

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:14.881
because of the threat

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:16.015
to civilian aircraft.

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:17.150
The decision was made to shoot

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.651
this one down right at the end.

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:20.320
We also got into the question of

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.120
the authorities

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:21.854
to carry out

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:22.822
something like this,

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:23.423
the NORTHCOM,

00:05:23.423 --> 00:05:24.791
NORTHCOM Mender would generally

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:26.092
have the authority

00:05:26.092 --> 00:05:26.793
to take out

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:29.028
or call a call a fighter jet to take out

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:31.331
an unidentified balloon over U.S.

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:32.231
airspace.

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:33.032
But Ryder said

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:35.301
because this doesn't pose a threat

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:37.203
to anybody below

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:37.870
or an imminent threat

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.305
to national security,

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:40.640
the decision went up to the president,

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:41.107
where President

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:42.909
Joe Biden gave his approval

00:05:42.909 --> 00:05:45.144
in that case, also worth noting,

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:45.745
as I suspect

00:05:45.745 --> 00:05:46.612
others have noted before,

00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:47.146
if you were listening

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:47.980
to the press conference,

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:49.415
it was the same type of aircraft

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:50.750
and the same type of missile

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.752
that was used to shoot this object down.

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:54.987
Major lines.

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:55.955
Certainly, we're trying to get

00:05:55.955 --> 00:05:58.591
as many details about this object,

00:05:58.591 --> 00:06:00.059
about the decision

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:01.561
to take it down as possible.

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:03.896
But can we just zoom out for a minute?

00:06:03.896 --> 00:06:05.732
This is the second time

00:06:05.732 --> 00:06:07.967
in, what, ten days now

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:11.904
that an object has been discovered in US

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:12.605
airspace.

00:06:12.605 --> 00:06:14.540
The first when a Chinese spy balloon

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:15.274
shot down.

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:17.643
Still so many questions about this one.

00:06:18.511 --> 00:06:20.313
What's your reaction to the breaking news

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:21.714
that we just learned minutes ago

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:23.649
and now just 2 hours ago,

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:25.585
this thing was shot down?

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:26.552
Well, Victor,

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:27.387
it tells me that

00:06:27.387 --> 00:06:28.488
they've changed their protocol

00:06:28.488 --> 00:06:29.155
in the fact

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:31.224
that they're going to notify

00:06:31.224 --> 00:06:31.891
the administration

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:33.960
or put the message out up front

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:34.894
and quickly

00:06:34.894 --> 00:06:36.562
decide and engage these targets.

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:37.997
And in a post-9-11

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:38.931
world, that's really

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:40.233
the only thing they can do.

00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:41.033
You know, that comment

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:42.535
the Pentagon makes about,

00:06:42.535 --> 00:06:42.702
you know,

00:06:42.702 --> 00:06:44.971
we wanted to see the last spy balloon

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:46.205
travel across the United States

00:06:46.205 --> 00:06:47.473
and get intelligence from it

00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:48.641
just frankly doesn't pass

00:06:48.641 --> 00:06:49.942
the red face test.

00:06:49.942 --> 00:06:51.677
So I think this was a message

00:06:51.677 --> 00:06:54.180
that they're sending out to the world

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.149
that we've got domain capability

00:06:56.149 --> 00:06:56.983
now to see this.

00:06:56.983 --> 00:06:58.050
It was at 40,000 feet.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:59.585
That was commercial airliners.

00:06:59.585 --> 00:07:00.987
But when the north commander last week

00:07:00.987 --> 00:07:02.722
said, you know, the last balloon

00:07:02.722 --> 00:07:03.589
showed some,

00:07:03.589 --> 00:07:03.890
you know,

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:04.891
domain weaknesses

00:07:04.891 --> 00:07:05.858
there, that's a problem.

00:07:05.858 --> 00:07:07.693
We usually don't tell our enemies

00:07:07.693 --> 00:07:09.328
where those those gaps are.

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:10.730
So I think this is a message

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:11.831
that was sent by the Pentagon.

00:07:11.831 --> 00:07:13.199
They've changed their protocol.

00:07:13.199 --> 00:07:14.333
They're going to do this from now on.

00:07:14.333 --> 00:07:15.067
This is going to be

00:07:15.067 --> 00:07:16.502
normal course of business.

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:19.172
If things violate our airspace. Hmm.

00:07:20.106 --> 00:07:21.774
Colonel, back to you.

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:23.142
I'm going to ask you a question

00:07:23.142 --> 00:07:25.945
that I assume maybe is tough to answer,

00:07:26.312 --> 00:07:28.714
but based on the description we have,

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:30.850
this is the size of a small car.

00:07:32.051 --> 00:07:35.521
It was about 40,000 feet non-removable.

00:07:36.322 --> 00:07:38.491
And when people here, smart, small cars

00:07:38.691 --> 00:07:40.693
don't think of the density of a car,

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:43.029
think of just the size of it.

00:07:43.029 --> 00:07:45.698
Is there anything that that you think

00:07:45.698 --> 00:07:48.468
that this could be likely is?

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:51.103
We can rule out that this item was

00:07:52.839 --> 00:07:54.440
Yeah, that's a great question, Victor.

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:55.775
I think that, you know,

00:07:55.775 --> 00:07:56.809
what are the possibilities?

00:07:56.809 --> 00:07:58.611
Frankly, there is actually a weather

00:07:58.611 --> 00:07:59.712
balloon, you know,

00:07:59.712 --> 00:08:00.079
so that

00:08:00.079 --> 00:08:02.748
we can't rule that out completely.

00:08:02.748 --> 00:08:05.384
The key thing that I focused on

00:08:05.384 --> 00:08:07.954
was that apparently this object

00:08:07.954 --> 00:08:10.490
did not have the kind of convective

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:12.825
capable ity that the balloon did.

00:08:13.426 --> 00:08:16.195
So that becomes a very different issue.

00:08:16.195 --> 00:08:17.129
And, you know, to

00:08:17.129 --> 00:08:19.932
what Major Lyons was saying, this

00:08:20.566 --> 00:08:21.467
there is a big difference

00:08:21.467 --> 00:08:22.702
from an intelligence collection

00:08:22.702 --> 00:08:23.703
perspective.

00:08:23.703 --> 00:08:26.739
It actually is okay in some cases

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:29.475
to collect the information.

00:08:29.675 --> 00:08:31.110
See, I would actually talk

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:32.645
to other entities.

00:08:32.645 --> 00:08:34.013
In this particular case,

00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:36.415
you have a bit of a different situation

00:08:36.415 --> 00:08:37.917
where it didn't talk to anything,

00:08:37.917 --> 00:08:39.785
but you don't know what a threat it poses

00:08:39.785 --> 00:08:41.654
except for the fact that, you know,

00:08:41.654 --> 00:08:44.023
it is a threat to commercial aviation.

00:08:44.023 --> 00:08:44.590
Hmm.

00:08:44.657 --> 00:08:46.292
Natasha, to you, in the intersection

00:08:46.292 --> 00:08:48.628
of the military and politics here,

00:08:48.628 --> 00:08:49.028
I think

00:08:49.028 --> 00:08:50.329
orange question is fair

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:54.267
considering that the argument that to let

00:08:54.267 --> 00:08:56.536
the Chinese balloon go across the country

00:08:56.536 --> 00:08:57.637
and then shoot it down,

00:08:57.637 --> 00:08:59.071
you can collect something from it

00:09:00.072 --> 00:09:01.407
One has to question the

00:09:01.407 --> 00:09:03.709
potency of the criticism

00:09:03.709 --> 00:09:05.211
of the administration

00:09:05.211 --> 00:09:06.646
for not shooting it down

00:09:06.646 --> 00:09:08.180
early on when it was discovered

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:09.649
that Chinese balloon

00:09:09.649 --> 00:09:12.184
and if that influenced

00:09:12.184 --> 00:09:14.854
the decision today.

00:09:14.854 --> 00:09:16.689
It's an absolutely fair question, Victor.

00:09:16.689 --> 00:09:18.624
And I think we should recap a little bit

00:09:18.624 --> 00:09:19.392
all of the furor

00:09:19.392 --> 00:09:21.561
that's happened over the last week

00:09:21.561 --> 00:09:22.428
from Republicans

00:09:22.428 --> 00:09:23.763
mainly who have wanted to know

00:09:23.763 --> 00:09:25.197
from the Biden administration

00:09:25.197 --> 00:09:26.699
why they didn't shoot down

00:09:26.699 --> 00:09:28.701
that first Chinese spy balloon

00:09:28.701 --> 00:09:30.870
when they saw that it was on a path

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:32.405
towards entering U.S. airspace.

00:09:32.405 --> 00:09:33.272
We know that Alaskan

00:09:33.272 --> 00:09:34.407
lawmakers in particular

00:09:34.407 --> 00:09:35.541
have been pretty angry

00:09:35.541 --> 00:09:36.542
with the Biden administration

00:09:36.542 --> 00:09:38.411
for allowing this balloon

00:09:38.411 --> 00:09:40.146
to cross over Alaska

00:09:40.146 --> 00:09:41.280
and then just deciding

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:42.315
that they were going to

00:09:42.315 --> 00:09:43.482
watch and monitor it

00:09:43.482 --> 00:09:44.417
because they did not think

00:09:44.417 --> 00:09:44.750
that it would

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:46.786
actually enter the lower 48.

00:09:46.786 --> 00:09:49.822
So that obviously has been taken

00:09:50.022 --> 00:09:51.324
by the Biden administration.

00:09:51.324 --> 00:09:51.691
They have been

00:09:51.691 --> 00:09:52.992
listening to that criticism.

00:09:52.992 --> 00:09:54.393
It is completely unclear

00:09:54.393 --> 00:09:55.595
at this point, of course,

00:09:55.595 --> 00:09:58.030
whether this was a decision that was made

00:09:58.197 --> 00:10:00.232
with that kind of criticism in mind.

00:10:00.499 --> 00:10:02.234
But it's also important to note here

00:10:02.234 --> 00:10:03.035
that we still do

00:10:03.035 --> 00:10:04.770
not know whether this item

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:06.005
or this device

00:10:06.005 --> 00:10:06.472
actually

00:10:06.472 --> 00:10:08.641
has any kind of intelligence value.

00:10:08.908 --> 00:10:10.376
It was unmanned,

00:10:10.376 --> 00:10:12.411
so it didn't pose any kind of risk to

00:10:12.712 --> 00:10:14.647
any human being inside the inside

00:10:14.647 --> 00:10:16.482
the object to shoot it down.

00:10:16.482 --> 00:10:19.118
But also it didn't pose any threats

00:10:19.151 --> 00:10:20.886
to appear to pose any threat

00:10:20.886 --> 00:10:22.154
to anyone on the ground.

00:10:22.154 --> 00:10:24.323
And it was traveling at an altitude

00:10:24.323 --> 00:10:25.758
that could have posed a threat

00:10:25.758 --> 00:10:26.759
to civilian aircraft.

00:10:26.759 --> 00:10:27.526
So there really was

00:10:27.526 --> 00:10:29.962
not as much of a choice here

00:10:29.962 --> 00:10:31.130
in what they were going to do

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:31.697
as they had

00:10:31.697 --> 00:10:32.365
with the balloon,

00:10:32.365 --> 00:10:33.432
which was traveling at around

00:10:33.432 --> 00:10:35.201
65,000 feet

00:10:35.201 --> 00:10:37.503
and did not appear to pose a real threat

00:10:37.503 --> 00:10:39.171
to any any civilians

00:10:39.171 --> 00:10:40.606
really, either in the air

00:10:40.606 --> 00:10:41.440
or on the ground.

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:42.808
So different situations here.

00:10:42.808 --> 00:10:43.576
I think it will be

00:10:43.576 --> 00:10:44.176
it'll be clearer

00:10:44.176 --> 00:10:45.211
once we actually are able

00:10:45.211 --> 00:10:45.678
to see

00:10:45.678 --> 00:10:46.746
during these recovery efforts

00:10:46.746 --> 00:10:47.747
what this is

00:10:47.747 --> 00:10:49.215
whether it was the correct decision.

